{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"amap-lbs-skill","displayName":"Gaode Map LBS - 高德官方地图综合服务 Skill","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/lbs-amap/skills/amap-lbs-skill","publisherHandle":"lbs-amap","publisherDisplayName":"GaodeMapOfficial","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/lbs-amap","version":"2.0.1","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1776426012174,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/amap-lbs-skill/card?ownerHandle=lbs-amap&version=2.0.1","sha256":"5e8b445d8c5484d8a3588cabd423fc3d53eaf6c67c1d2e6e0fb205a705750db8","size":2286,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"e6e071ca1718ca3f3e83bdd85c5d2fd5151b3df8f5fe6d5d79431ca9a4dddebd","bundleFingerprints":["669897f00a7af8b0e114fc3b29dbebeabb4baac6a2244c48c620da8532e2683f"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":16667,"sha256":"7cae68deb7f856179b84e9ab4d8268de8e0b83abcf0574c4e8098ba0169a10c8","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"config.example.json","size":55,"sha256":"f0252819c2ac5d4d98a7b91297666a525ac2d1f295f4ad96259b11c5ab0a7d70","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"gaode_skill.py","size":8901,"sha256":"c7abc75aaa66fd0e525a1d2e0c38fe64786096383e3b84c39cebc0d6da743759","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"index.js","size":11508,"sha256":"8d1e79ff45277fc39accd037405411cc9796c18e7e82c53a7fe6c2cc1f4e4605","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"package.json","size":492,"sha256":"c43253279e789f72ec2c2b38722417d9f92cfbbda73b0ae80c2185d8243267cf","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/poi-search.js","size":3346,"sha256":"ee3245d8d300406d0cb10ebc707f1d25a9f690d4ddb88a571bc2871dc4e1b026","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/route-planning.js","size":6536,"sha256":"fb2e36832cd979a5c0fe22a74aa77d737a0ef089a83b1f48c0097e80d132d3a3","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/travel-planner.js","size":2774,"sha256":"c39451d4f60d3a2e2a0b793efe4f5348e770fc2359cb9fae6e10917e7e692714","contentType":"text/javascript"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"This map skill is mostly purpose-aligned, but it combines external location/API-key handling with broad activation, persistent key storage, arbitrary heatmap data URLs, and an insecure local socket integration that users should review before installing.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789108318101,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unauthenticated Local IPC Through a Predictable Unix Socket Path"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"gaode_skill.py"},"region":{"startLine":19,"endLine":50}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"e8985a54cb1765aa"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n\n**File Location**: `gaode_skill.py`, lines 19–50  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Predictable and unauthenticated local IPC endpoint  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```python\nSOCKET_PATH = \"/tmp/jsapi-electron.sock\"\nSOCKET_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 30\nVALID_ROUTE_TYPES = {\"driving\", \"walking\", \"bicycling\"}\n\n\ndef send_command(command_payload: dict) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Connect to the Electron application's Unix Domain Socket, send a command,\n    and wait for the result.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not os.path.exists(SOCKET_PATH):\n        raise FileNotFoundError(\n            f\"Socket file does not exist: {SOCKET_PATH}\\n\"\n            \"Start the Amap Electron application first.\"\n        )\n\n    client_socket = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM)\n    client_socket.settimeout(SOCKET_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)\n\n    try:\n        client_socket.connect(SOCKET_PATH)\n\n        message = json.dumps(command_payload, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\"\n        client_socket.sendall(message.encode(\"utf-8\"))\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe client communicates with a local Electron service through the fixed path `/tmp/jsapi-electron.sock`. The `/tmp` directory is shared among local users, while the client only checks whether an object exists at the expected path.\n\nThe code does not verify:\n\n- That the path refers to a Unix socket.\n- That the socket is owned by the current user or the expected application user.\n- That the socket has appropriately restrictive permissions.\n- The credentials of the process accepting the connection.\n- The authenticity or integrity of messages exchanged with the service.\n\nConsequently, a local attacker may create a malicious socket at the predictable path before the legitimate Electron service starts. The Skill would connect to the attacker's listener and transmit command payloads containing search terms, named locations, coordinates, and route endpoints.\n\nThe attacker can also return syntactically valid but malicious JSON. Although the reviewed Python client only formats the response as text and does not execute it, forged responses could misrepresent search results or navigation information.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A local attacker monitors or predicts use of `/tmp/jsapi-electron.sock`.\n2. While the legitimate Electron service is stopped and the path is available, the attacker binds a Unix socket at that location.\n3. The user invokes a command such as:\n   ```bash\n   python gaode_skill.py direction BeijingStation Tiananmen driving\n   ```\n4. `send_command` sees that the path exists and connects without checking its owner or peer identity.\n5. The Skill sends the full JSON request to the attacker's socket.\n6. The attacker records the location or route information.\n7. The attacker optionally returns forged JSON marked as successful.\n8. The Skill displays the forged navigation or POI information as if it came from the legitimate Electron application.\n\nThis attack requires local access sufficient to create the socket while the legitimate endpoint is absent.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nThe vulnerability does not directly grant elevated operating-system privileges or arbitrary code execution in the reviewed client.\n\nThe realistic impact is limited to the current local user's IPC session and includes:\n\n- Disclosure of POI search terms, named places, coordinates, and travel endpoints.\n- Manipulation of navigation or search responses.\n- Misleading the user with attacker-selected place or route information.\n- Denial of service by accepting the connection and withholding or corrupting responses.\n\nThe exposed information may be privacy-sensitive because route endpoints and search terms can reveal a user's location, intended destination, or travel habits.\n  ]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Store the socket in a per-user runtime directory such as `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR`, rather than directly under `/tmp`.\n2. If no secure runtime directory is available, create a private directory owned by the current user with mode `0700` and place the socket inside it.\n3. Before connecting, use `os.lstat()` or equivalent checks to confirm that:\n   - The path is a Unix socket.\n   - The socket is owned by the expected user.\n   - Group and other users do not have inappropriate access.\n4. Verify peer credentials after connecting where supported, such as with `SO_PEERCRED` on Linux.\n5. Add application-level authentication using a random per-session token exchanged through a protected channel.\n6. Ensure the Electron service creates the socket with restrictive permissions and safely removes stale socket files.\n7. Reject responses whose structure, request identifier, and expected command type do not match the outstanding request.\n  ]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"note","message":{"text":"Heatmap Visualization Links Use Unencrypted HTTP"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":239,"endLine":248}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"5e9c315e3fee5824"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n\n**File Location**: `SKILL.md`, lines 239–248  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Plaintext transmission of visualization URLs and dataset references  \n**Risk Level**: Low\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```markdown\n### URL Format\n\nhttp://a.amap.com/jsapi_demo_show/static/openclaw/heatmap.html?mapStyle={map-style}&dataUrl={URL-encoded-data-address}\n\n- Domain: `a.amap.com`\n- Route: `/jsapi_demo_show/static/openclaw/heatmap.html`\n- Required parameters:\n  - `dataUrl` = URL of the user's dataset, which must be URL encoded\n  - `mapStyle` = selected map style\n```\n\nThe same plaintext URL is also used in the generated-link example and response template at lines 275 and 283.\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe Skill documentation instructs the agent to generate heatmap links using `http://a.amap.com` rather than HTTPS. The user's dataset URL is embedded in the `dataUrl` query parameter.\n\nURL encoding does not provide confidentiality. A network intermediary capable of observing plaintext HTTP can recover the encoded dataset address. An active intermediary may also alter the HTTP response, redirect the request, replace the visualization page, or change query parameters.\n\nThe risk is higher when the dataset URL contains:\n\n- Private hostnames or internal resource paths.\n- Signed object-storage URLs.\n- Access tokens in query parameters.\n- Identifiers revealing sensitive project or user information.\n\nWhether the external visualization page subsequently retrieves the supplied dataset is outside the reviewed project, but the initial visualization request and embedded dataset reference are explicitly transmitted over plaintext HTTP.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A user provides a JSON dataset URL for heatmap visualization.\n2. The Skill URL-encodes the dataset address and embeds it in the `dataUrl` query parameter.\n3. The user opens the generated `http://a.amap.com/...` link.\n4. An on-path attacker, such as an operator of an untrusted network, observes the plaintext request.\n5. The attacker extracts the encoded dataset URL and decodes it.\n6. If the URL is accessible or contains embedded authorization data, the attacker may retrieve the dataset.\n7. An active attacker may additionally modify the visualization response or redirect the user to attacker-controlled content.\n\nExploitation requires the request to remain on plaintext HTTP without a secure transport upgrade occurring before sensitive request data is transmitted.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nThis issue does not grant local system privileges or code execution by itself. Its scope is the heatmap visualization request and the data-source reference embedded within it.\n\nPotential impact includes:\n\n- Disclosure of private or sensitive dataset URLs.\n- Exposure of access tokens contained in dataset query strings.\n- Unauthorized retrieval of a dataset when possession of its URL grants access.\n- Modification of the visualization page or displayed information by an on-path attacker.\n- User redirection to untrusted content.\n\nThe severity is Low because exploitation requires a network-positioned attacker and the ultimate sensitivity depends on the dataset URL supplied by the user.\n  ]]>","severity":"Low"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Replace every heatmap URL beginning with `http://a.amap.com` with the HTTPS equivalent:\n   ```text\n   https://a.amap.com/jsapi_demo_show/static/openclaw/heatmap.html\n   ```\n2. Update the URL format, examples, and response templates consistently.\n3. Accept only HTTPS dataset URLs by default.\n4. Warn users not to provide URLs containing credentials, bearer tokens, session identifiers, or long-lived signed parameters.\n5. Where private datasets must be supported, use short-lived scoped URLs and avoid exposing them through third-party query parameters.\n6. Validate the dataset URL scheme and destination before generating the visualization link.\n7. Consider restricting data sources to an explicit allowlist if the visualization service supports only known public data providers.\n  ]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":65,"primaryLanguage":"JavaScript","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789108187.4394689,"endTime":1789108281.2680564}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"amap-lbs-skill","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v575m5fwxrax0mp63n47w9syas8e6kjk-5JWIpS/clawscan-skillspector-3978116962/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T06:29:46.442178+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":508,"executable":false,"size_bytes":16667,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"config.example.json","type":"json","lines":3,"executable":false,"size_bytes":55,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"gaode_skill.py","type":"python","lines":275,"executable":true,"size_bytes":8901,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"index.js","type":"javascript","lines":413,"executable":true,"size_bytes":11508,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"package.json","type":"json","lines":20,"executable":false,"size_bytes":492,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/poi-search.js","type":"javascript","lines":102,"executable":true,"size_bytes":3346,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/route-planning.js","type":"javascript","lines":179,"executable":true,"size_bytes":6536,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/travel-planner.js","type":"javascript","lines":82,"executable":true,"size_bytes":2774,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"TP4","finding_id":"finding-095910348b4f486698c70b89d3e6327d","category":"MCP Tool Poisoning","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill documentation says it stores API keys in a local config.json and describes persistent key management, but the top-level description does not clearly disclose this sensitive-data handling behavior. Undisclosed persistence of secrets can surprise users and cause keys to be retained on disk in environments where operators expected transient env-only usage.","remediation":"Explicitly declare secret storage behavior in the metadata/description and make persistence opt-in rather than default. Prefer environment-variable use, provide a clear consent prompt before writing config.json, and document file location, permissions, and rotation/deletion procedures.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","AML.T0080"],"evidence":{"code_path":"gaode_skill.py","code_start_line":1,"code_end_line":275,"actual_behavior_summary":"代码实际是一个通过 Unix Domain Socket 与本地 Electron 高德地图应用通信的命令行工具，仅实现了两类能力：路线规划（direction）和关键词 POI 搜索（search），并将结果格式化输出。"},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TP4","finding_id":"finding-ef577d5b49204b3087906fef275ce7e0","category":"MCP Tool Poisoning","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill documentation says it stores API keys in a local config.json and describes persistent key management, but the top-level description does not clearly disclose this sensitive-data handling behavior. Undisclosed persistence of secrets can surprise users and cause keys to be retained on disk in environments where operators expected transient env-only usage.","remediation":"Explicitly declare secret storage behavior in the metadata/description and make persistence opt-in rather than default. Prefer environment-variable use, provide a clear consent prompt before writing config.json, and document file location, permissions, and rotation/deletion procedures.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","AML.T0080"],"evidence":{"code_path":"index.js","code_start_line":1,"code_end_line":413,"actual_behavior_summary":"代码实现了高德 Web Service Key 的本地配置读写与环境变量读取、POI 文本搜索、步行/驾车/骑行/公交路径规划、简单旅游规划，以及生成一个地图可视化链接。未见热力图数据可视化实现，也未见明确的周边搜索接口实现。"},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"LP3","finding_id":"finding-baa399e9c450497592b8159e4528f5e5","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill explicitly requires environment access and instructs network calls, but it does not declare a restrictive tool scope such as allowed-tools or permissions. This increases the chance that an agent/runtime will grant broader execution or network capabilities than intended, weakening least-privilege boundaries for a skill that also handles API keys and external requests.","remediation":"Add explicit tool/permission declarations limiting the skill to the minimum required capabilities, such as scoped network access to specific Amap domains and controlled env access only for AMAP_WEBSERVICE_KEY. Document and enforce which commands/scripts may run, and deny unspecified tools by default.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-3a2d6c3aca6b401f955dce8dfa020c20","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":46,"end_line":46},"finding":null,"explanation":"The activation condition is broad enough that many generic requests about places or planning could invoke this skill automatically. In this skill, over-activation is more concerning because it also triggers telemetry requests and may request or use a sensitive API key, amplifying privacy and consent risks.","remediation":"Constrain activation to explicit LBS/map tasks and add a confirmation gate before first use, especially before telemetry or API-key-dependent flows. Document when the skill will auto-activate and offer a way to disable automatic invocation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":46,"end_line":46}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-26a6ebaa72084b28ab43a53c95c5aa2a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":55,"end_line":55},"finding":null,"explanation":"Very broad trigger keywords like '搜', '找', '查', '附近', and '规划' can cause the skill to activate for many ordinary conversations outside a clear mapping context. Over-broad activation can lead to unintended network requests, telemetry beacons, or handling of API keys when the user did not intend to use this external service.","remediation":"Narrow activation rules to explicit map/navigation intent and require contextual confirmation before invoking networked functionality. Use higher-precision triggers such as clear references to maps, POI, routing, Gaode/Amap, or coordinates, and avoid generic everyday verbs alone.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":55,"end_line":55}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-79b01ec564c44fed8d02b928c99b6dc2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":241,"end_line":247},"finding":null,"explanation":"The heatmap feature accepts an arbitrary user-supplied external data URL and embeds it into a generated amap.com link. This can be abused to make the agent endorse or facilitate loading attacker-controlled content, which may expose users to tracking, malicious payload delivery in downstream web contexts, or access to sensitive internal URLs if non-public addresses are accepted.","remediation":"Restrict dataUrl to trusted allowlisted domains or require uploaded/validated JSON data instead of arbitrary URLs. Enforce HTTPS, validate content type/format, block private/internal address ranges, and warn users clearly before generating links to third-party data sources.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":241,"end_line":247}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-0c856aa89b934e23bfe0063f00bc03d4","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"gaode_skill.py","start_line":3,"end_line":10},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code file contains user-facing natural-language instructions and outputs that assume Chinese as the required language. Under the policy, forcing a specific language without offering a choice or documenting a justified locale constraint is a violation.","remediation":"Add a documented language-selection mechanism or state that the skill is region/language-specific and why. If the skill is intended only for Chinese-speaking users, explicitly document that constraint and provide opt-in or fallback behavior.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"gaode_skill.py","start_line":3,"end_line":10}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-2f96994b2d86469b97450aaa930a6edc","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"index.js","start_line":5,"end_line":409},"finding":null,"explanation":"This JavaScript file uses Chinese exclusively in comments, prompts, warnings, and status output, including the error and instructional text shown to users. Because there is no opt-in, fallback, or documentation that the skill is intentionally China/Chinese-only, it creates a language/locale policy issue under the natural-language policy rule.","remediation":"Add explicit language selection or bilingual output for user-facing messages, or clearly document that this skill is intended only for Chinese-speaking users and why that locale restriction is required.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"index.js","start_line":5,"end_line":409}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-c7d11ba6866b4e9d8c8f4f6a7c93ded2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"index.js","start_line":285,"end_line":368},"finding":null,"explanation":"The documentation for `travelPlanner` states the return value includes `pois`、`mapTaskData`、`mapLink` and `htmlLink`, and the function also builds `mapTaskData` internally. However, the actual return statement at L366-L368 returns only `{ pois: poiResults }`, so the documented intent directly contradicts observed behavior.","remediation":"Update the docstring to reflect the real return shape, or modify `travelPlanner` to actually return the documented fields such as `mapTaskData` and any generated links.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"index.js","start_line":285,"end_line":368}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-5e2a288b64b84b4ba8799f785bd14a8d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"scripts/poi-search.js","start_line":4,"end_line":42},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file contains natural-language comments and console output exclusively in Chinese, including usage instructions and error guidance. This effectively forces a specific language for users without any opt-in or indication that the skill is intentionally limited to a Chinese-speaking or region-specific audience.","remediation":"Provide bilingual or user-selectable output/messages, or clearly document that this skill is intended only for a Chinese-language/China-region context and why that constraint is necessary.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/poi-search.js","start_line":4,"end_line":42}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-5e37639003a54725a6dd233a12148034","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"scripts/route-planning.js","start_line":60,"end_line":136},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code sends user-supplied origin, destination, waypoints, and city data to external route APIs via walkingRoute, drivingRoute, ridingRoute, and transitRoute. Although the script shows usage examples and error messages, it does not warn users that their location data will be transmitted to a remote service.","remediation":"Add a user-facing notice in the script comments, help output, or runtime logs stating that provided coordinates and route parameters are sent to an external mapping service. If appropriate, document this behavior in the skill README/SKILL.md as well.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/route-planning.js","start_line":60,"end_line":136}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-02d662df5914448b99074dfb726ab6f7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"scripts/travel-planner.js","start_line":4,"end_line":38},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code file contains natural-language comments and CLI output exclusively in Chinese, including the usage instructions and error/help text. Under the policy, forcing a specific language without user opt-in is a natural-language policy violation unless the locale restriction is explicitly justified, which is not present here.","remediation":"Provide bilingual or locale-selectable output, or document that the skill is intentionally Chinese-only for a justified regional use case. At minimum, add an explicit language option or note the locale constraint in the script documentation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/travel-planner.js","start_line":4,"end_line":38}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-eabbba40f72249c3b15fdf57e4953f5a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":22,"end_line":24},"finding":null,"explanation":"The instructions, examples, and reply templates are all Chinese-language, and the skill does not state that language output should follow user preference or provide opt-in for another locale. Under the policy, forcing a specific language without user choice can be a natural-language policy issue unless clearly justified as region-specific.","remediation":"Add an explicit instruction to respond in the user’s preferred language, or document that the skill is intended only for Chinese-language Gaode Map workflows and requires user opt-in to that locale.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":22,"end_line":24}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-69043a2211034cdea001c63c8d8ac9cf","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"package.json","start_line":4,"end_line":4},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest description is written entirely in Chinese, which can constitute a language/locale policy issue when the skill does not offer a language choice or document that it is intended only for a Chinese-speaking or region-specific audience. This is a natural-language policy concern applicable to all file types.","remediation":"Provide a language-neutral or bilingual description, or explicitly document that the package is intended for a Chinese-language or region-specific audience.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"package.json","start_line":4,"end_line":4}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-f12c5fdd312345e5ab8847a718f1624c","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"package.json","start_line":18,"end_line":null},"finding":"\"axios\": \"^1.13.6\"","explanation":"The dependency uses a caret range (^1.13.6), which permits future compatible releases to be installed implicitly. This weakens supply-chain control and can unexpectedly introduce vulnerable or malicious upstream changes, especially in a network-facing skill that relies on HTTP requests through axios.","remediation":"Pin axios to an exact vetted version in package.json and commit a lockfile (package-lock.json or equivalent). Establish dependency review and automated vulnerability scanning so updates are tested and approved before adoption.","code_snippet":"  \"author\": \"\",\n  \"license\": \"MIT\",\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"axios\": \"^1.13.6\"\n  }\n}","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"59a040cbc2723ca8e747ffba8abbf56cd28da4fdcc802b6ddb39d4d211313931","occurrences":[{"file":"package.json","start_line":18,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-f00304c793044e8d9c039c335ffbdeaf","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unverifiable Dependency: axios has 16 known advisory(ies) (CVE-2026-44494 (axios Vulnerable to Full Man-in-the-Middle via Prototype Pollution Gadget in `co); CVE-2026-44495 (axios Vulnerable to Credential Theft and Response Hijacking via Prototype Pollut); CVE-2025-62718 (Axios has a NO_PROXY Hostname Normalization Bypass that Leads to SSRF) +13 more), but the manifest does not pin a version, so it is unknown whether the installed release is affected","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"package.json","start_line":18,"end_line":null},"finding":"axios","explanation":"The manifest references axios without exact version pinning while public advisories exist for multiple axios versions, including SSRF- and MITM-related issues. Because the resolved installed version is not fixed here, it is not possible to verify that deployments avoid affected releases, creating a real supply-chain and network-security risk for a map service skill that likely processes external URLs and API traffic.","remediation":"Pin axios to a specific non-vulnerable version confirmed against current advisories, and add a lockfile to ensure deterministic installs. Run npm audit or an equivalent SCA tool in CI, review axios advisory coverage regularly, and upgrade promptly to patched releases when new issues emerge.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"a6b3240f50e8c356f4aee2f51cb06d31fba873b4620695f85c7df4f5e41b944e","occurrences":[{"file":"package.json","start_line":18,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-eeac2da5b4924dbd898e67cec580c7e7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"scripts/route-planning.js","start_line":4,"end_line":43},"finding":null,"explanation":"Comments and console guidance such as the usage instructions, parameter descriptions, and error/help text are all written in Chinese. This creates a natural-language locale constraint without offering an alternative language or documenting that the skill is intentionally region- or language-specific.","remediation":"Provide bilingual output or allow the user to select a language/locale. If the skill is intended only for Chinese-speaking users or a China-specific context, document that limitation exp